#!/usr/bin/env bash

lord --verbose << "EOF"
Run a diff -r on the directories eng/ and com/.

eng/ is the current default english translation, as markdown.
com/ is the current default english translation, as markdown, with any commentary I happen to have written while out walking away from my laptop.

Whenever you find a bit of commentary in com/ that isn't in eng/, I want you to:

1. Find the corresponding book, chapter, and verse in [01][0-9]*/*.tex
2. Add the commentary for each such verse in com/ to the lualatex files there.
3. Be idempotent: If you find a verse already has the same commentary in the .tex file version of a verse that it has in com/, then do nothing for that verse.
4. If you see 'A: ...' in the commentary, make that \aA{...} in the LaTeX, replacing the content virtually identically.
5. But not exactly identically, b/c I want you to make any minor tweaks needed to make the markdown commentary into proper LaTeX.

EOF
